<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa's Weber sees staff accepting measures.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa's Weber sees staff accepting measures.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa chief executive Juergen Weber said on Wednesday he believed staff at the German airline would accept restructuring measures aimed at reducing management and administration jobs by a minimum 10 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe these measures will be viewed positively by our employees,&quot; Weber said after speaking at a Frankfurt conference on the airline industry.</p>
<p>Weber declined further comment on the restructuring measures announced earlier on Wednesday that will reduce management and administration costs ahead of the liberalisation of the European airline industry slated for April 1.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
